            <ArticleTitle>Diagnosing and treating the patient with restricted mandibular opening: a new approach.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>245-51; quiz 252, 264</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Patients with a restricted mandibular opening and related pain require a systematic process for differential diagnosis and treatment planning. This article considers the differential diagnostic process, treatment planning, and treatment delivery for a patient seeking a second opinion before surgery for a closed lock. A closed lock occurs when the disc in the joint has been pulled off the head of the condyle and forward, blocking the condyle from translating forward.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
